WEBVTT

00:00:01.917 --> 00:00:19.158
Around the World in 80 Days by Jules Verne Chapter 1 It is London in 1872.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:38.525
And this is Mr. Phileus Fog's house.

00:00:38.585 --> 00:00:44.980
Mr. Phileus Fog is an English gentleman.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.054
He lives in London.

00:00:49.114 --> 00:00:54.700
He hasn't got a wife or children.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:02.698
but he has got a French servant, Pas Partou.

00:01:02.758 --> 00:01:09.483
Fogg goes to his club every day.

00:01:09.543 --> 00:01:14.836
He eats at his club at 12 o'clock.

00:01:14.896 --> 00:01:20.780
In the afternoon, he reads there.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:27.780
In the evening, He eats there again.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.640
Then he talks with his friends.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.682
And at midnight, he goes home.

00:01:37.742 --> 00:01:42.242
Pass Part 2 is happy.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:46.914
He wants a quiet job.

00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:53.954
But one evening, fog sees something interesting.

00:01:54.014 --> 00:01:56.473
in the Times.

00:01:56.533 --> 00:02:05.976
Gentlemen Thief takes £5,000 from the Bank of England.

00:02:06.036 --> 00:02:12.230
At the club, Fogg's friends talk.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:20.318
That Gentlemen Thief can't go far, says Ralph.

00:02:20.378 --> 00:02:23.795
trains and ships.

00:02:23.855 --> 00:02:28.677
Today's detectives move fast.

00:02:28.737 --> 00:02:36.100
But thieves can move fast too, Flanagan says.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:46.579
Today you can go round the world in 80 days, says Fogg.

00:02:46.638 --> 00:02:57.036
Do it, and I pay you £20,000, says Stuart.

00:02:57.096 --> 00:03:03.278
I'm leaving tonight, Otz's fault.

00:03:03.338 --> 00:03:14.913
Perhaps I can't do it, Stuart, but then I pay you £20,000.

00:03:14.972 --> 00:03:24.926
The train for France leaves before 9 in the evening.

00:03:24.986 --> 00:03:34.508
Fog must be back in London by the 21st of December.

00:03:34.568 --> 00:03:43.129
Fog gives £20,000 in a bag to his servant.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:48.181
We're leaving for France, he says.

00:03:48.241 --> 00:03:53.266
Pass Part 2 isn't very happy.

00:03:53.326 --> 00:03:59.051
They go to France.

00:03:59.111 --> 00:04:14.114
Then they take a train to Italy and a ship to Port Side in Egypt.

00:04:14.174 --> 00:04:26.402
When their ship arrives in Suiz, an English detective, Mr. Fix, is waiting.

00:04:26.462 --> 00:04:31.466
He's looking for the gentleman thief.

00:04:31.525 --> 00:04:36.730
Fog visits the passport office.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:41.023
Mr. Fix sees him there.

00:04:41.083 --> 00:04:46.790
It's the gentleman thief, he thinks.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:50.164
I must tell London.

00:04:50.224 --> 00:04:54.586
Chapter 2 Fix looks at past Part 2.

00:04:54.646 --> 00:04:56.427
Where are you going?

00:04:56.487 --> 00:05:07.261
He asks.

00:05:07.321 --> 00:05:22.178
around the world," says Paspartou.

00:05:22.237 --> 00:05:28.864
But right now I need some new shirts.

00:05:28.924 --> 00:05:36.179
Fix takes him to a shop and leaves him there.

00:05:36.239 --> 00:05:42.354
Then he sends a telegram to London.

00:05:42.414 --> 00:05:48.338
The gentleman thief is going to Bombay.

00:05:48.398 --> 00:05:49.888
Stop.

00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:53.062
Fix.

00:05:53.121 --> 00:06:07.252
Later, he gets on the ship for Bombay with Vogue and Paspartou.

00:06:07.311 --> 00:06:15.686
It is the 20th of October.

00:06:15.746 --> 00:06:22.800
They all arrive in Bombay, two days early.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:32.015
At 4.30 in the afternoon, Phog and Paspartou leave the ship.

00:06:32.075 --> 00:06:39.250
They want to get a train across India to Calcutta.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:43.990
It leaves at 8 o'clock.

00:06:44.049 --> 00:06:50.030
First, Phog goes to the passport office.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:54.713
Then he eats at the station.

00:06:54.773 --> 00:07:01.596
Paspar II visits the temple at Malibar Hill.

00:07:01.656 --> 00:07:06.550
But he doesn't take off his shoes.

00:07:06.609 --> 00:07:10.240
The priests get angry.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:17.965
They take his shoes and Paspartou runs away.

00:07:18.025 --> 00:07:27.682
Fog and Paspartou get on the train.

00:07:27.742 --> 00:07:35.358
But Fix stays in Bombay.

00:07:35.417 --> 00:07:41.586
He is waiting for a telegram from London.

00:07:41.646 --> 00:07:49.698
After three days, the train stops.

00:07:49.758 --> 00:07:59.909
The railway from Colby to Alalabad isn't ready.

00:07:59.969 --> 00:08:05.893
Some men are building the railway.

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:15.177
but there are 80 kilometers without a railway between Colby and Alalabad.

00:08:15.237 --> 00:08:21.792
In Colby, Paspartu gets some new shoes.

00:08:21.852 --> 00:08:30.600
He also finds an elephant to take them to Alalabad.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:36.055
They stop near a temple.

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:44.180
In the village of Pilaji, the old Indian prince is dead.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:53.605
His young wife, the princess, must die with him in a big fire.

00:08:53.665 --> 00:09:00.868
We must help that woman, says fall.

00:09:00.928 --> 00:09:05.156
The priests start the fire.

00:09:05.216 --> 00:09:10.666
Through the smoke, fog sees something beautiful.

00:09:10.726 --> 00:09:19.001
The prince stands up and takes the princess out of the fire.

00:09:19.061 --> 00:09:24.504
The prince and the princess come nearer.

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:29.668
Fog sees that the man is not the prince.

00:09:29.728 --> 00:09:34.926
It is Paspar II in the prince's clothes.

00:09:34.986 --> 00:09:41.026
Quickly, let's go, says Paspar 2 to fog quietly.

00:09:41.086 --> 00:09:47.688
Suddenly, the priests see the prince's body on the fire.

00:09:47.748 --> 00:09:57.744
They see that the man in the prince's clothes is not the prince, and they become angry.

00:09:57.804 --> 00:10:07.336
Forg, Paspar II, and the Princess leave very quickly on the elephant.

00:10:07.397 --> 00:10:35.976
Chapter 3 At last, they arrive in Alalabad fog buys some European clothes for the princess.

00:10:36.036 --> 00:10:42.060
What a beautiful woman, he thinks.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:50.668
On the train going to Calcutta, she speaks for the first time.

00:10:50.728 --> 00:10:54.821
My name's Mrs. Auda.

00:10:54.881 --> 00:10:57.708
Thank you for helping me.

00:10:57.768 --> 00:11:01.736
But I don't know what to do now.

00:11:01.796 --> 00:11:05.798
I can never go home.

00:11:05.858 --> 00:11:10.182
We can take you to Hong Kong.

00:11:10.243 --> 00:11:12.044
Fogg says.

00:11:12.103 --> 00:11:16.076
Thank you, says Mrs. Aouda.

00:11:16.136 --> 00:11:20.170
I have a cousin there.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:27.262
At Calcutter Station, a policeman stops them.

00:11:27.322 --> 00:11:31.242
He takes them to see a judge.

00:11:31.302 --> 00:11:35.566
Mrs. Oder goes too.

00:11:35.626 --> 00:11:39.528
Fix is in Calcutta.

00:11:39.589 --> 00:11:45.284
Detectives must move fast to find gentleman thieves.

00:11:45.344 --> 00:11:48.456
He's waiting in court.

00:11:48.516 --> 00:11:53.410
But fog and his friends don't see him.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:56.788
Why are we here?

00:11:56.848 --> 00:12:04.144
for breaking the rules in a temple, says the judge.

00:12:04.204 --> 00:12:19.968
In Pilaji, asks Vogue, no, in Bombay, says the judge, and he puts Paspatu's shoes on the table.

00:12:20.028 --> 00:12:27.702
You must go to prison for this, says the judge.

00:12:27.762 --> 00:12:36.756
But Fogg gives two thousand pounds to the court, and they're free again.

00:12:36.816 --> 00:12:41.898
They get onto the ship for Hong Kong.

00:12:41.958 --> 00:12:45.118
Fix follows them.

00:12:45.178 --> 00:12:48.739
But Paspartu sees him.

00:12:48.799 --> 00:12:54.368
Perhaps he's a detective, he thinks.

00:12:54.428 --> 00:13:03.786
Perhaps he's working for Mr. Stewart from the Gentleman's Club in London.

00:13:03.846 --> 00:13:13.719
In Hong Kong, Mrs. Aouda learns that her cousin now lives in Holland.

00:13:13.779 --> 00:13:19.810
Come with us to Europe, Fox says.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:27.392
Paspatu wants to buy three tickets on the Carnatic.

00:13:27.452 --> 00:13:33.723
It leaves for Yokohama in Japan the next morning.

00:13:33.783 --> 00:13:42.775
But at the ticket office, he learns that it's leaving early that evening.

00:13:42.835 --> 00:13:48.916
Paspatu meets Fix near the ticket office.

00:13:48.976 --> 00:13:51.758
Come for a drink.

00:13:51.818 --> 00:13:54.360
says Fix.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:14:08.812
Fix tells Paspar II, I think your Mr. Fog is a gentleman thief and I want to arrest him.

00:14:08.872 --> 00:14:22.078
Paspar II doesn't want to help Fix, but the detective buys drink after drink.

00:14:22.138 --> 00:14:31.476
Paspartou goes to sleep on the table.

00:14:31.536 --> 00:14:39.702
Now he can't tell fog about the Carnatic things fix.

00:14:39.762 --> 00:14:46.222
It leaves tonight, but without fog.

00:14:46.282 --> 00:14:51.500
Chapter 4 Later, Paspar 2 wakes up.

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:54.672
He goes onto the Carnatic and the ship leaves.

00:14:54.692 --> 00:15:09.158
But Fogg and Mrs. Oda aren't with him.

00:15:09.218 --> 00:15:29.906
Next morning, Fogg and Mrs. Oda go to get on the Carnatic, but it isn't there.

00:15:29.966 --> 00:15:32.587
Fix arrives.

00:15:32.647 --> 00:15:38.040
The Carnatic's on its way to Japan, he says.

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:43.522
And the next chip to Yokohama leaves next week.

00:15:43.582 --> 00:15:46.283
Where's Passpartou?

00:15:46.343 --> 00:15:48.749
asks Mrs. Oda.

00:15:48.809 --> 00:15:55.478
I don't know," says Fog, but we must go on without him.

00:15:55.538 --> 00:15:59.021
We must find another ship.

00:15:59.081 --> 00:16:05.736
Fog finds a small ship, the Tanka Deer, to go to Shanghai.

00:16:05.796 --> 00:16:10.800
There they can get a big ship to Yokohama.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:13.702
Can I go with you?

00:16:13.762 --> 00:16:15.482
asks Vix.

00:16:15.542 --> 00:16:17.084
Of course.

00:16:17.144 --> 00:16:24.156
Fog answers.

00:16:24.216 --> 00:16:35.158
The Tankardir travels through storms.

00:16:35.219 --> 00:16:41.740
And at last arrives near Shanghai.

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:46.891
Suddenly they see a big ship in front of them.

00:16:46.951 --> 00:16:50.362
It's on its way to Yokohama.

00:16:50.422 --> 00:17:01.221
Signal to that ship, says Fog.

00:17:01.281 --> 00:17:14.533
Passpartu arrives in Yokohama, but he has no money.

00:17:14.593 --> 00:17:25.700
He leaves the Carnatic and finds work in Mr. Batulka's circus.

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:35.228
I can go to America with the circus, he thinks.

00:17:35.288 --> 00:17:42.234
Fog, Mrs. Oda, and Fix get on the big ship.

00:17:42.294 --> 00:17:49.466
And a week later they arrive in Japan.

00:17:49.526 --> 00:17:55.928
The Carnatic is in Yokohama.

00:17:55.989 --> 00:18:01.260
Fog and Mrs. Oda go on to the Carnatic.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:10.766
They find Paspartou's name in the book of passengers' names, but they can't find Paspartou.

00:18:10.826 --> 00:18:16.060
Their ship leaves for San Francisco in a few hours.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:21.415
Before they leave, Fog goes to the circus.

00:18:21.475 --> 00:18:24.958
Paspartou sees him there.

00:18:25.018 --> 00:18:26.870
Mr. Fog!

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:30.800
He says happily.

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:36.981
Phog wants to take Paspar II with him.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:44.844
But first, he must pay Mr. Batulka.

00:18:44.904 --> 00:18:58.801
At six o'clock in the evening, Phog, Paspar II and Mrs. Auda go on to the American ship.

00:18:58.861 --> 00:19:08.016
Fix follows them.

00:19:08.076 --> 00:19:22.703
Chapter 5 I'm sorry about Hong Kong, says Paspar 2.

00:19:22.763 --> 00:19:27.116
I don't usually drink much, but...

00:19:27.176 --> 00:19:33.300
Later, Paspar 2 sees fics on the ship.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:39.476
My master isn't a gentleman thief, he says.

00:19:39.536 --> 00:19:43.378
Listen, says Fix.

00:19:43.438 --> 00:19:49.302
I now have papers from London to arrest Mr. Fogg.

00:19:49.363 --> 00:19:52.594
But I can't stop him now.

00:19:52.654 --> 00:19:55.696
It must be in England.

00:19:55.756 --> 00:20:10.338
When we get there, They arrive in San Francisco in the morning.

00:20:10.398 --> 00:20:15.519
The New York train leaves that evening.

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:22.052
Fog and Mrs. Oder meet Fix in the street.

00:20:22.112 --> 00:20:25.732
I am travelling to Europe now.

00:20:25.792 --> 00:20:28.884
Can we travel together?

00:20:28.944 --> 00:20:30.454
He asks.

00:20:30.514 --> 00:20:35.343
Of course, answers Fog.

00:20:35.403 --> 00:20:39.731
They walk into a meeting.

00:20:39.792 --> 00:20:42.862
Camel feel for judge.

00:20:42.923 --> 00:20:45.614
Shout the people on the left.

00:20:45.674 --> 00:20:48.604
Mandy boy for judge.

00:20:48.664 --> 00:20:51.875
Shout the people on the right.

00:20:51.935 --> 00:20:56.176
Then they start fighting.

00:20:56.236 --> 00:21:06.679
One man wants to fight fog, but fix, stands in front of him and stops him.

00:21:06.739 --> 00:21:13.160
Paspartou finds it all very strange.

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:19.774
So, Mr. Fix is helping us now, he thinks.

00:21:19.834 --> 00:21:28.877
Fog, Mrs. Aude, Paspartou and Fix get on the train that evening.

00:21:28.937 --> 00:21:40.584
They cross one old bridge very fast and it falls into the river behind them.

00:21:40.644 --> 00:21:47.899
Then, some Sioux Indians arrive.

00:21:47.959 --> 00:21:50.790
They kill some passengers.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:54.022
Passpartu fights them.

00:21:54.082 --> 00:22:01.134
But they take him and ride away with him.

00:22:01.194 --> 00:22:09.756
Fog, Mrs. Elder, and Fix get off the train.

00:22:09.817 --> 00:22:14.600
Fog goes to look for Passpartu.

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:18.854
He finds him and brings him back.

00:22:18.914 --> 00:22:26.948
But they must wait until evening, until the next train to New York.

00:22:27.008 --> 00:22:33.470
How can we travel fast over the snow?

00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:35.442
Thinks fix.

00:22:35.502 --> 00:22:39.744
On a slench with sails.

00:22:39.804 --> 00:22:44.200
Soon they arrive in Omaha.

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:49.395
There, they take a train to New York.

00:22:49.456 --> 00:22:55.878
They arrive in New York 45 minutes late.

00:22:55.938 --> 00:23:06.936
Their ship, the China, is on its way to Liverpool.

00:23:06.996 --> 00:23:32.819
Chapter 6 The next morning, fog, Mrs. Auda, Paspartou and fix, leave on a small ship, the Henrietta, going to France.

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:52.634
Later, Fogg gives the sailors money and they agree to go to Liverpool, not to France.

00:23:52.694 --> 00:23:58.267
The sailors lock the captain in his room.

00:23:58.327 --> 00:24:05.890
The Henrietta is in the middle of the Atlantic and there's no coal.

00:24:05.950 --> 00:24:12.511
Burn all the wood on the ship, says Fogg.

00:24:12.571 --> 00:24:24.046
The ship arrives in Queenstown, in the south of Ireland, and there's no more wood on it.

00:24:24.106 --> 00:24:32.782
Let's get off here, says Fog, to Mrs. Aouda, Pasparto, and Fix.

00:24:32.842 --> 00:24:37.456
Fix doesn't arrest Fog in Queenstown.

00:24:37.516 --> 00:24:42.730
He's waiting for them to arrive in England.

00:24:42.790 --> 00:24:47.962
They get on a train and travel to Dublin.

00:24:48.022 --> 00:24:53.362
There, they get a fast ship to Liverpool.

00:24:53.423 --> 00:25:02.504
In Liverpool, fix arrests Fogg at last and takes him to prison.

00:25:02.564 --> 00:25:08.645
In prison, Fogg looks at his diary.

00:25:08.705 --> 00:25:13.814
At two o'clock, he looks at his watch.

00:25:13.874 --> 00:25:24.016
There's time to go to London on a fast train and to be at my club by 8.45 this evening.

00:25:24.076 --> 00:25:26.318
He thinks.

00:25:26.378 --> 00:25:34.720
At half-past three, Fix arrives with Mrs. Oder and Passpartou.

00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:39.721
I'm sorry, Mr. Fog, says Fix.

00:25:39.782 --> 00:25:45.344
The gentleman thief, James Strand, is in prison.

00:25:45.404 --> 00:25:48.568
You're free to go.

00:25:48.628 --> 00:25:54.794
Angrily, fog punches fix in the face.

00:25:54.854 --> 00:26:02.962
Then fog, Mrs. Aude and Paspartou run to Liverpool station.

00:26:03.022 --> 00:26:07.006
They get a fast train to London.

00:26:07.066 --> 00:26:12.009
The train arrives at ten minutes to nine.

00:26:12.069 --> 00:26:20.683
Fogg is five minutes late for his meeting with Stuart.

00:26:20.743 --> 00:26:34.293
Fogg doesn't want to get to his club late, so he goes home with Mrs. Aouda and Paspartou.

00:26:34.353 --> 00:26:43.630
Around the world in 80 days and 5 minutes, he's the loser.

00:26:43.690 --> 00:26:53.074
He has only £20,000 in the bank, and he must give it all to Stewart.

00:26:53.134 --> 00:26:59.666
I'm sorry for bringing you here to a poor man's home.

00:26:59.726 --> 00:27:03.544
He says to Mrs. Aude the next morning.

00:27:03.605 --> 00:27:06.052
Will you marry me?"

00:27:06.112 --> 00:27:08.404
asks Mrs. Aouda.

00:27:08.464 --> 00:27:12.294
Yes, says Fogg.

00:27:12.355 --> 00:27:18.507
That afternoon, Fogg tells Passpartou.

00:27:18.527 --> 00:27:25.149
I want to marry Mrs. Aouda tomorrow, the 23rd of December.

00:27:25.209 --> 00:27:30.810
Can you speak to the people at Marliman Church about it?

00:27:30.870 --> 00:27:34.947
Soon, Passpartou returns.

00:27:35.007 --> 00:27:38.994
Today's the 21st of December.

00:27:39.054 --> 00:27:45.897
When you travel east around the world, you get an extra day.

00:27:45.957 --> 00:27:50.859
You aren't late for your meeting at the club after all.

00:27:50.919 --> 00:27:53.740
But you must run.

00:27:53.800 --> 00:27:59.694
At a quarter to nine, Vogue enters his club.

00:27:59.754 --> 00:28:03.275
I win, he says, to Stuart.

00:28:03.335 --> 00:28:07.170
Where's my £20,000?

00:28:07.230 --> 00:28:15.043
Next Monday, fog, the world traveler, marries Mrs. Oda.

00:28:15.103 --> 00:28:17.758
He's a very happy man.

